{"ts": 0.062739, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97menv 1 — variables\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nA \u001b[36mvariable\u001b[0m is a name that holds a value. The shell swaps\r\n", "len": 101}
{"ts": 0.062773, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[92m$name\u001b[0m for the value before it runs the line.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[92mecho $HOME\u001b[0m           \u001b[90m# a variable the shell already has\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mpet=owl\u001b[0m               \u001b[90m# set one: no spaces around =\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mecho $pet\u001b[0m            \u001b[90m# prints owl\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92menv | head\u001b[0m            \u001b[90m# the first lines of the variable list\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92menv | grep '^pet='\u001b[0m    \u001b[90m# prints nothing\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nNotice that \u001b[92mpet\u001b[0m is missing from the list. A variable you set\r\nis private to this shell until you export it (lesson 2).\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Try the five lines, then type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 599}
{"ts": 0.066315, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mnext\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(go on)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(this screen again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mprev\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(back)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 159}
